data: {"sections":[{"section_id":"header","type":"template","content":"LEGAL NOTICE\n(Under Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908)\n\nDate: 04 May 2026\n\nTo,\nThe Executive Engineer, Bihar Road Construction Department, Government of Bihar\nVishweshwaraiya Bhawan, Bailey Road, Patna - 800015\n\nFrom,\nM/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd.\nThrough: Adv. Anjali Verma, Advocate\nChamber No. 42, Patna High Court Bar Association, Patna - 800001","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"subject_line","type":"template","content":"Subject: Legal Notice under Section 80 CPC — prior to institution of suit against the Government / Public Officer\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nUnder instructions from and on behalf of my client, M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd., I hereby serve upon you this legal notice under Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908, and call upon you to note the following:","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"body","type":"ai_generated","content":"1. My client M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd. is a company incorporated under the Companies Act, 2013, having its registered office at Industrial Area, Patna, Bihar, and is engaged in the business of construction and infrastructure development works. The company has been undertaking various government construction projects across Bihar with an impeccable track record and has established itself as a reliable contractor in the field of road construction and allied works.\n\n2. My client M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd. was awarded a contract for construction of culverts on NH-31 vide Work Order No. BRCD/PAT/2024/118 dated 12.06.2024 issued by your office for a total contract value of Rs. 2,75,00,000/- (Rupees Two Crores Seventy Five Lakhs only). The said work order contained detailed specifications, timelines, and terms and conditions for execution of the construction work as per the approved technical specifications and quality standards.\n\n3. My client diligently commenced the construction work immediately upon receipt of the work order and executed the entire project with utmost professionalism, adhering to all technical specifications, quality parameters, and safety norms prescribed under the contract. The construction work was carried out under the supervision and monitoring of the site engineer appointed by your department, who regularly inspected the progress and quality of work being executed.\n\n4. My client successfully completed all the contracted work by 28.02.2026 in accordance with the terms and conditions of the work order and submitted the final running bills along with measurement books duly signed and certified by the site engineer posted at the project site. The completion of work was duly verified and accepted by the competent technical officers of your department, and all requisite clearances and approvals were obtained as per the contractual obligations.\n\n5. Despite completion of the work and submission of all required documents, my client has repeatedly requested for release of the final payment through various communications dated 05.03.2026, 22.03.2026, and 18.04.2026, copy of which are enclosed herewith for your ready reference. However, you have failed and neglected to release the outstanding final payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- (Rupees Eighty Seven Lakhs Fifty Thousand only) which has remained due and payable since 28.02.2026.\n\n6. The wrongful withholding of the legitimate payment due to my client has caused severe financial hardship, operational difficulties, and reputational damage to my client's business operations. The delayed payment has disrupted my client's cash flow, affecting its ability to service existing commitments and undertake new projects, thereby causing quantifiable financial loss and damage to business reputation in the construction industry.\n\n7. I am constrained to serve this legal notice upon you in compliance with the mandatory provisions of Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908, which requires service of two months' prior notice before instituting any suit against the Government or a public officer in respect of any act purporting to be done in official capacity.\n\n8. You are hereby called upon to release the outstanding payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- along with applicable interest within a period of two months from the date of service of this notice, failing which my client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate legal proceedings against you and the State Government for recovery of the said amount along with interest, damages, and costs, without any further reference to you in the matter."},{"section_id":"demand_clause","type":"template","content":"DEMAND\n\nYou are hereby called upon to release the outstanding payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- along with interest at the rate of 12% per annum from 28.02.2026 till actual payment, and pay damages of Rs. 5,00,000/- for the wrongful withholding within a period of two (2) months from the date of receipt of this notice, failing which my client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate legal proceedings before the competent civil court, at your risk, cost, and consequences, without any further reference to you.","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"closing","type":"template","content":"A copy of this notice is retained in my office for record and further action.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\n_________________________\nAdv. Anjali Verma\nAdvocate\nEnrollment No. BCB/4521/2018\nChamber No. 42, Patna High Court Bar Association, Patna - 800001\n\n(Counsel for M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd.)","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"disclaimer","type":"template","content":"AI-assisted draft — verify with applicable law before filing. Lawie does not provide legal advice.","alignment":"center","style":"footer_small_gray"}]}

event: checklist
data: {"items":["Send via Registered Post AD (Acknowledgement Due) — retain receipt","Send additional copy via Speed Post","Retain photocopy of notice with postal receipts","Keep proof of delivery (AD card) safely — needed at time of filing suit","Wait mandatory 2 months from date of receipt before filing suit","Attach all supporting documents referenced in the notice","Verify noticee's correct designation and office address"]}

